r me over here  if you  pay attention to my type of scraper you  see how it gathers most of the depth and  pushes all the water away  so the pressure washer helps losing more  debt in a rug  pressure washing a rag alone cannot get  all the debt out you need a shampoo to  help do its magic it's not a one  procedure thing  so i gave it a good old rinse with a  squeegee  then we flipped it to the back  it's important to clean the work area so  the depth doesn't come back into the rug  then you can continue with working  the back side will also require putting  shampoo on it  it's the same procedure just that that  [ __ ] doesn't take as long as the top  side because usually the dirt is trapped  more on the top side than the back side  when you clean the back some of the dead  somehow goes back to the top part so you  have to flip it up and redo the whole  process again  so  scrub scrub scrub  eventually you realize the water becomes  clear so once it gets clear you know  your grag is clean now  patient rugs are not too delicate if i  may say there are different types of  patient rugs some require very close  attention to cleaning but some will  require the normal cleaning procedure  this one needed  extra care because because of the  fringes especially if you're not careful  the fringes are just going to come out  so you manually have to apply the  shampoo  with the chemicals onto the fringes then  you manually scrub  i can use any brush to clean the fringes  any hard brush it has to be a hard brush  because you're dealing with years of  depth you need a hard brush to be able  to scrub all that out  then i use the power washer to blow the  depth out of it  so i am using a wet vacuum to vacuum  most of the water out of the rack i  repeat the process like twice i'm able  to get at least 80 to 90 percent of the  water out of the rug before i leave it  out to try  i see some people use the centrifuge  machine where it spins all the water out  i believe those who use that machine  don't have very good weather over there  in my country the sun is always out so  it helps dry the rocks quickly  it came out great the client was very  satisfied the original colors were  restored as well i had no idea how the  original colors look like you're unable  to tell how originally it looks like so  you're done cleaning  it's usually dead sitting in there for  years that makes it heavily swell it's  best to have a vacuum in your household  where once in a while you vacuum all the  debt out of your rug  [Music]  a rug like this can be cleaned every  half a year  you

